=== Strategy to Raise From KOS ===

1. Create a new character who isn't KOS, or ask a non-KOS friend for help.

2. Have them go to the Hall of Sorcery and find [[Daenor Casthopur]].

3. Say "Tell me about Neclo." to receive the Lore Quest item, which is ''not'' No-Drop.

4. Transfer the note to your KOS character.

5. Go to [[Qeynos Hills]] and be a high enough level above [[Neclo Rheslar ]] that he will not attack you when you approach him.

6. Put the note in trade, drink a [[Cloudy Potion]] or have a friend cast invisibility on you, then hit Accept ... .

7. Repeat steps 2-6 until you are are considered dubious in wolf form

8. Do [[Unsar's Glory]] instead

=== Skeleton Strategy ===

This strategy involves spam-hailing [[Den Magason]] and [[Kazlo Naedra]] when they get close to each other, giving 2g to Den in exchange for a [[Blank Scroll Sheets]] (which is LORE), then giving Kazlo the scroll for reputation.

1. Have access to a skeleton illusion; [[Lich]], [[Amulet of Necropotence]], etc. This will bring you to Dubious with the Order of Three even as something like an Iksar Necromancer.

2. Head to the bank and withdraw 299 platinum and convert it into gold (by having the platinum on your cursor and clicking on the gold in your inventory).

3. Find [[Den Magason]] who is only in Qeynos during the daylight hours. Try and find him near -110, 46, as this is where Kazlo will eventually path close to. He will give you a [[Blank Scroll Sheets]] in exchange for 2g. They are '''lore''' but also droppable. The reason having ~2990 gold is useful here is that you can simply hit backspace 3x & then hit enter to withdraw 2g.

4. [[Kazlo Naedra]] will eventually path close to [[Den Magason]]'s spot at the docks. Lock the two in place near each other by spam hailing them.

5. Hand the purchased [[Blank Scroll Sheets]] to [[Kazlo Naedra]], then buy another from [[Den Magason]]. Repeat ad-nauseam.

If preferred, you can also purchase scrolls from Den & then drop them over and over, then pick them up and hand them to Kazlo. This is probably a bit easier on the hands and only requires you to hail lock one NPC in place at a time.